Inspection response
    Existing object identifier, class, methods and instance variables.
    Runtime record: host, process, worker, active calls, references, pulse timing, metrics.
    Retention record: root flag, sampled path, unavailable objects and interpretation note.
Call activity
    Identifier, chain, selector, target, executing-or-waiting state and start time.
MCP request and response
    Preserve JSON-RPC identifier and version, method/params or result/error.
MCP tool invocation and result
    Named tool with typed argument payload; text content with execution-error flag.
MCP initialization
    Proposed protocol version, capabilities and client implementation name/version.

InspectResponse adds methodSignatures: selector to ordered parameter names.

NavigationMethod records class, selector, parameters, sends, source, file, line and foreign status. NavigationIndex contains methods and source errors.

WorkspaceResult carries typed result, output and optional error. ObjectWorkspaceRequest carries receiver ID and code. BlockDef optionally captures a selfOverride Value.

InteractionRequest/Result describe typed UI calls. InteractionRecord adds timestamp/class. ResultRequest binds/releases handles. RecordingRequest/Response supplies structured records and exports. InspectorViewRequest/Response supplies target, key and JSON layout.

Define DebugRequest, DebugCommand, DebugSnapshot, DebugHTTPRequest/Response, TraceEvent, TraceSnapshot and TraceRequest as documented in SPEC. Add sender to MessageRequest and optional debug to RuntimeInspection.

SourceRequest carries action/class/source/digest/revision/message. SourceResponse carries canonical file/current source/digest/readOnly/revisions/historicalSource/diff/gitObject/errors. SourceRevision carries ID/unix timestamp/subject.

SpawnRequest optionally carries NativeSnapshot. NativeDefinition/Snapshot and PrototypePatch/Method describe loaded native copies. WireDefinition/Node/Input and WireRun/WiringResponse describe typed message graphs and reports. RuntimeInspection adds prototype and definitionVersion.

PromiseSnapshot carries state, typed target/arguments/result, error, timestamps and reply timeout. InteractionRequest accepts an optional timeoutMs for promise interactions.

WorkbenchDefinition/Tool describe live toolbar actions; WorkbenchResponse and ExamplesResponse carry object identities and editable catalog data.

SelectorSpan/Site describe parsed Unicode source locations. RefactorRequest supplies selectors and optional class; RefactorFile/Edit/Response carry digests, proposed sources, per-line edits, literal references and errors.

Add ControlProperties (wire properties), ControlState (serialized properties/children) and ControlPlan (validated reconciliation tree).
